{"name":"San Francisco Pink","hex":"#bb33aa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"san","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sanskrit."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Ancient Greek letter representing /s/ (uppercase Ϻ, lowercase ϻ), originally used in some dialects instead of sigma."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/san"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"San Francisco","blocks":[{"text":"San Francisco, officially the City and County of San Francisco, is the 17th-most populous city and second-densest large city in the United States, with a population of 826,079 in 2025. It is the fourth-largest city in California. Some 4.6 million residents live in the city's metropolitan statistical area, which is the 13th-largest in the United States. Around 9.2 million live in the San Jose–San Francisco–Oakland combined statistical area, the fifth-largest in the United States. San Francisco is a global center for technology and finance, and is well-known for its affluence, eclectic architecture, and mild climate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Zeppelin-ride-020100925-195_%285029394846%29.jpg/330px-Zeppelin-ride-020100925-195_%285029394846%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco"},{"title":"Francisco","blocks":[{"text":"Francisco is the Spanish and Portuguese form of the masculine given name Franciscus."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francisco"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the colo